---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Gear from '../components/Gear.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Technical advisory · {SITE.location}</p>
      <h1>Systems that stay maintainable.</h1>
      <p class="thesis">Helping organisations own their technology instead of renting it.</p>
      <p>{SITE.tagline}</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/consulting/">Consulting services</a>
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Gear size={288} />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap intro">
    <p>Maintainable systems and repairable machines are the same idea: owning your tools and being able to fix them. The consulting applies it to organisations today. The research applies it to the machines that will work alongside us. Either way, you should be able to walk away with your data, your software and the knowledge of how it works. See the <a href="/principles/">principles</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cards" aria-label="What we do">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Consulting</h2>
      <p>Independent advice on technology, data, automation and AI. It starts from the problem, not the product.</p>
      <a href="/consulting/">Services →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Heritage</h2>
      <p>Archive, catalogue and search systems that archives, societies and museums own outright, with maintenance you can leave at any time.</p>
      <a href="/heritage/">The offer →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Research</h2>
      <p>Long-term work on robotics for archaeology: field data capture, <a href="/provenance/">provenance</a> and machines that can be repaired.</p>
      <a href="/research/">Direction →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Notes</h2>
      <p>Working notes on projects, methods and the tools behind them.</p>
      <a href="/notes/">Read →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
